# SurfBud — Project Overview

SurfBud is an AI-powered browser productivity platform. It has three independent deployable units inside one GitHub repository.

## Repository Structure

```
surfbud/
├── api/          Node.js + Express + TypeScript backend
├── dashboard/    React + Vite + TypeScript frontend
├── extension/    Chrome Extension Manifest V3 + TypeScript
└── docs/         All project documentation
```

Each folder is a fully independent project with its own `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, and deployment pipeline. They share NO build-time code — only runtime communication through HTTPS REST and WebSocket.

## Tech Stack

### api/
- Node.js + Express + TypeScript
- MongoDB + Mongoose (persistent storage)
- Redis (cache + BullMQ queues + pub/sub)
- Socket.IO (WebSocket server)
- BullMQ (async job queues)
- Zod (runtime validation)
- JWT (auth — access token 15min + refresh token 7d)
- Groq SDK (AI inference — multi-model fallback chain)

### dashboard/
- React 18 + Vite + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS (utility-first styling)
- Recharts (all data visualizations)
- Zustand (global state)
- React Query (server state + caching)
- Socket.IO Client (WebSocket)

### extension/
- Chrome Manifest V3
- React (side panel + popup)
- Chrome Side Panel API (primary UI surface)
- Chrome Downloads API
- Chrome Tabs API
- Service Worker (background processing)

## Shared Types

Each folder has `src/types/shared/` — identical TypeScript type definitions copied across all three. If you change a shared type in one folder, always update all three in the same change.

## Non-Negotiable Architecture Rules

1. Controllers import Services only — never Repositories or Models directly
2. Services import Repositories + other Services — never raw DB queries
3. Repositories import Models only — zero business logic inside
4. No raw MongoDB queries outside repository files
5. No business logic outside service files
6. AI calls NEVER happen in request-response cycle — always via BullMQ queue
7. Metrics are NEVER calculated on demand — always read from pre-materialized UserMetrics document
8. WebSocket pushes deltas only — never full dataset refreshes

## Current Phase

Phase 1 — Full product build. No Free/Pro tier distinction. All features for all users. Monetization is deferred.
